Best Practice for Maven + Tomcat
Do not copy:



.git/
target/
*.log
into the Docker image unless required.

Create .dockerignore:



.git
target
*.log
Then use a multi-stage build:



FROM maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-17 AS build
 
WORKDIR /app
 
COPY . .
 
RUN mvn clean package
 
FROM tomcat:9.0
 
COPY --from=build /app/target/*.war \
/usr/local/tomcat/webapps/ROOT.war
 
EXPOSE 8080
 
CMD ["catalina.sh","run"]
This is the approach typically used in Jenkins → Docker → Kubernetes → ArgoCD pipelines because the final image contains only the WAR file and Tomcat, making it much smaller and more secure.





